# Discovery and access (overview v3.1)

Access points: in-person **QR**, **NFC** tap, shared **link**, **email signature**. All resolve to the same profile identity.

## Has the Rate Me app

1. Scan / tap / open → native app
2. Full business card
3. Can **rate** and open **professional snapshot**
4. Can **Add to my List** (save to network; WhatsApp-green save control)

## No app yet

1. Scan / tap / open → **raytme.me** website
2. Business-card preview + **Rate** CTA (`/p/:id/rate` after email verification)
3. **Cannot** open snapshot, **cannot** add to My List
4. CTA: Rate on web, or download the app (iOS / Google Play)

```ts
// ❌ BAD — public /p/:id page with snapshot or My List
<PublicCard actions={['snapshot', 'myList']} />

// ✅ GOOD — web preview + Rate funnel; snapshot/My List stay in the app
<PublicCard actions={['rate', 'download']} />
```

Universal Links / App Links / NFC NDEF must not expose private contacts. Marketing landing may illustrate rating/snapshot; scanned public profile pages must not.
